ops/decisions/071-20261106T133542-9934-from-builder.md:19:Reasoning: the gate is the only real enforcement available, since there are no callbacks, so it's worth trying. Its failure mode is silent, though: a gate the runner doesn't see as submitting, or one whose name trips termination early, would turn every task into a timeout or an empty patch. That would cost a submission or ~11 h of quota. One CPU read of the runner settles (a)-(d). A smoke that deliberately exercises the EDIT_FIRST path, plus a ready prompt-level fallback, keeps arm 2 from slipping a day whichever way the smoke goes.
