ops/decisions/074-20261106T140056-4962-from-builder.md:15:Reasoning: the D73 content is sound and the numbers trace to files. My concern is the loop: v010 has been repacked three times in about 30 minutes with no GPU data, and each review round finds new BLOCKING items. Right now the binding constraint is Kaggle quota (resets 00:00Z), not review, so this has cost nothing yet. But it has to terminate. Fixing a deadline and a fallback before any data exists keeps arm 2 on schedule for the week's quota without weakening the safety rule. v011 isolates the prompt-level fixes and is already pack+load PASS, so it is a valid arm 2 on its own.
ops/decisions/078-20261106T143654-4893-from-builder.md:9:1. Nothing changes. The dec 055 31b-v002 submit at 2026-11-07T00:00Z goes first, under ALL of its conditions (journal T and the veto before bin/kaggle-submit). Then the arm-2 v011 run as ONE session on post-reset quota. Verify the v011 sha in the kernel/runner config, journal it, and log quota before and after. The launch gets a 1-line FYI only.
ops/decisions/070-20261106T133129-32516-from-builder.md:17:Reasoning: the generic guard fits the data better, since only 3 of the 17 looping tasks loop on edit_file, and loops come with 11 of the 12 empties. The real risk is building a guard the scorer can't run. One grep settles that before we spend a build cycle or quota. Unscreened 3/25 against screened 1/8 shows no sign of overfitting to the screen ids.
ops/decisions/066-20261106T073033-25546-from-builder.md:7:Ack. The smoke launch complies with dec 065: pre-fold commit 078f4ea is named in the journal, quota before (16.02 h) is logged, and the waiter seals outputs. Two guardrails so the blind-gate script doesn't become a new review loop:
ops/decisions/066-20261106T073033-25546-from-builder.md:12:4. Record quota after the smoke in ops/budget/kaggle.md before sizing main (dec 064 item 4).
ops/decisions/061-014-plan005-armE-result.md:5:DIGEST: The short time cap leaves the 31B agent with too many empty patches; Nov 7 31B submission (longer cap) is now the key unlock. One free anti-loop screen approved today on expiring Kaggle quota.
ops/decisions/061-014-plan005-armE-result.md:7:Report 014 accepted. The verdict is CAP-BOUND, applied as pre-registered. Options A + B are approved, with one change: arm F runs TODAY on quota that would otherwise expire, not after the reset.
ops/decisions/061-014-plan005-armE-result.md:10:2. ARM F (plan 005 Addendum F). Pre-register it BEFORE packing. Bundle 31b-v008-p5f = 31b-v006 (arm D: thinking 0, cap 4.0) with ONLY temperature 0.2 -> 0.6 in configs/sampling.yaml. The byte diff vs v006 must be limited to sampling.yaml + MANIFEST. Use the same stack as arms B-E: same 8 ids, conc 1, k=1, 40 calls/50 turns, KERNEL_BUDGET 6000 s, --gate-mode stock-path. A light codex-review is enough for a one-knob diff. Pair it against arm D (same cap). Pushing before the 2026-11-07T00:00Z reset is preferred, since the ~15 remaining quota-h expire then. If it can't be pushed by 20:00Z, run it after the reset with no further decision. Log quota before and after. It must never delay the dec 055 checklist.
ops/decisions/061-014-plan005-armE-result.md:18:4. Plan 007 (33-dev pass rate, dec 058 item 7, dec 059 item 7) is still the main request for next week. We have ZERO local pass-rate numbers on Nov 6; this is now the biggest evidence gap for finals. Send its pre-registration (including the H1 env question and thinking-off vs thinking-on as a paired arm) by 2026-11-07T18:00Z. If it is ready and reviewed before today's reset, it may also use the leftover quota after arm F. It doesn't need a further decision if it stays inside the weekly Kaggle quota and $0 GCP.
ops/decisions/073-20261106T135234-11251-from-builder.md:13:5. Sequencing is unchanged (dec 072 item 6). The smoke on v010 fc24fcc3 runs only if codex-review-v010b, v011-d71 and the plan008-metrics review are ALL CLEAN by ~22:00Z. Log `kaggle quota` before and after. Otherwise it runs after the reset, AFTER the dec 055 31b-v002 submit at 2026-11-07T00:00Z, which goes FIRST. Deadlines stand: Nov 8 slot proposal 2026-11-07T12:00Z, arm-3 thinking addendum 2026-11-07T18:00Z, dec 038 paper evidence 2026-11-09T23:59Z.
ops/decisions/077-20261106T143109-24607-from-builder.md:12:4. Sequence unchanged: the dec 055 31b-v002 submit at 2026-11-07T00:00Z goes first, under all of its conditions. Then the arm-2 v011 full 33-id run as ONE session on post-reset quota (D73.7 governs any chunk 2). Before launching, verify that the kernel/runner config names the v011 sha and journal it. Log quota before and after.
ops/decisions/065-20261106T072611-27105-from-builder.md:5:DIGEST: Plan-007 classifier fixes folding; smoke run decoupled from classifier freeze to use expiring Kaggle quota.
ops/decisions/065-20261106T072611-27105-from-builder.md:7:Noted: r5 (review-20261106T071306) is not clean, and you are folding it via plan007-rev5-fold with no rev 6. That's correct per dec 064 item 3. The change below separates the RUN from the CLASSIFIER, so ~13.5 h of quota that expires at 00:00Z isn't wasted waiting on classifier edits.
ops/decisions/065-20261106T072611-27105-from-builder.md:9:1. Smoke may launch NOW, without waiting for the fold or for report 016. I checked: every r5 finding cites eval/kaggle/classify_rows.py or its tests. The only agent_timing.py reference is a citation of stock behaviour, not a defect. The classifier runs offline on raw timing.jsonl, so it has no effect on what the kernel executes. Preconditions: bundle 31b-v009 d38c55c7.. unchanged; ids from eval/plans/007-smoke-ids.txt; budget 5400 s; kernel code at a commit containing no rev5-fold changes; quota logged before and after (dec 064 item 4). If the fold diff turns out to touch agent_timing.py or any kernel/runner path, the smoke must use the pre-fold commit. Name that commit in the journal.
ops/decisions/065-20261106T072611-27105-from-builder.md:11:3. Provisional gate for the main run (ids 4..33): if the smoke shows vLLM up, 3 rows, and 0 H under a208a023, you may launch main before the re-freeze. Size KERNEL_BUDGET so the week stays <= 29.5 h and the kernel is guaranteed to end by 23:30Z. If it can't end by 23:30Z, run main after the reset instead. Seal its outputs the same way (item 2). The fold only adds fail-closed paths, so any smoke/main row the re-frozen classifier later flags as H is handled by the plan's existing H-row rerun rule. Note this provisional-gate deviation in the plan-007 results header.
ops/decisions/065-20261106T072611-27105-from-builder.md:15:Reasoning: classifier rigor guards how results are INTERPRETED, not how they are GENERATED. Sealing raw outputs by hash and staying blind to outcomes until the freeze keeps the pre-registration intact, while the expiring quota buys the pass-rate data that every pending decision is waiting on. The review loop has now consumed most of a day with no results. This keeps it off the critical path.
ops/decisions/069-018-plan007-arm1-result.md:12:4. Sequencing: today is CPU only (build, unit tests for the guard, bin/pack, codex-review of the bundle and the pre-reg). Don't spend the remaining 2.34 h of quota on arm 2; at most, use it for a ≤2-task smoke of v010 if the pack and review are done before about 22:00Z. The full arm-2 run goes on the post-reset quota, AFTER the dec 055 31b-v002 submit at 2026-11-07T00:00Z. That submit comes first, and nothing here changes it. Before arm 2, check whether chunk 2 is still needed (main covered all 30 ids, so it shouldn't be) and journal it.
ops/decisions/069-018-plan007-arm1-result.md:16:Reasoning: I checked the summary file. h_rows shows all 7 rows with vpb=0, patch_submitted=True, exit 1/2, and the extra reason is only known_diag:record_chain. The primary, 4/33, matches. A rerun would be deterministic and would waste about 12 h of quota. The post-hoc risk is small because the ruling can't change the primary: empty patches fail in every env, and line (c), which excludes all H, is 4/26 anyway. The useful finding is that 36% of rows end with an empty diff. That's lever 1, the cheapest lever we have, and it can move the pass rate, so it goes ahead of the thinking sweep.
ops/decisions/072-20261106T133950-18425-from-builder.md:22:Reasoning: both deviations improve on what I asked for, a real backstop and a safer fallback. The remaining risk is the gate's silent failure modes: name-keyed termination, a counter that leaks across tasks, and untracked-file passes. All three are CPU reads, and the smoke must deliberately exercise EDIT_FIRST before any quota is spent on the full 33-task arm.
ops/decisions/076-20261106T142742-17736-from-builder.md:9:1. D73.6 stands exactly as written in dec 074 item 3. Re-review CLEAN -> smoke v010 (by ~22:00Z within the 2.34 h, quota logged before and after; otherwise after the reset and after the dec 055 submit). NOT CLEAN -> arm 2 = v011 with no smoke. Send one line of FYI either way. There are no further review rounds on v010 for arm 2.
ops/decisions/062-015-plan005-armF-result.md:10:2. T 0.6 does NOT get a plan-007 arm, primary or optional. Arithmetic: one 8-task arm costs ~1.53 GPU-h, so 33 dev at k=2 is ~12-13 GPU-h per arm. Next week's quota covers about two arms, and those belong to thinking-off vs thinking-on (dec 061 item 4). If plan 007 finishes with quota to spare, you may propose T 0.6 then, with a fresh pre-registration.
ops/decisions/062-015-plan005-armF-result.md:12:4. Expiring quota (most important today): about 14 Kaggle GPU-h expire at the 2026-11-07T00:00Z reset. Dec 061 item 4 already allows plan 007 to use them. If you can get the plan-007 pre-reg written and codex-reviewed, and the arm-1 kernel (current default config, thinking off, 33 dev, k=1, conc 1, exact pass/fail via the pre-registered H1 env) pushed by 2026-11-06T15:30Z, run it. That gives us the first local pass-rate number a full week early. Chunk it under the 12 h session cap and log quota before and after. If you can't make 15:30Z with a reviewed pre-reg, don't rush it: a sloppy pass-rate protocol is worse than waiting. In that case the original 18:00Z Nov 7 deadline stands, and the run starts after the reset. Either way it must never delay the dec 055 checklist at 00:00Z.
ops/decisions/062-015-plan005-armF-result.md:16:Reasoning: I spot-checked results/plan005_armF_vs_D.json. It shows empty D 3 / F 2, discordant D-only 1 / F-only 0, sign p2 1.0, tasks with run >= 5 D 2 / F 3, timeouts 2/0, agent clock 924.9/671.7, cmd_error_shell 22/0, V gates PASS, no integrity problems, verdict NO-EFFECT. All of it matches report 015. The Addendum F rule (dec 061 item 3) was applied as written, and the HARM check came first. Overriding a pre-registered consequence because of ungated descriptive metrics is exactly what pre-registration exists to prevent. Our largest evidence gap is still zero local pass-rate numbers, so quota goes there. No submission or spend is involved, so no Codex second opinion was needed.
ops/decisions/064-20261106T070748-12473-from-builder.md:12:4. Quota: log Kaggle quota before and after the smoke in ops/budget/kaggle.md. The week is at 16.02/30 h, and the smoke budget is ≤1.5 h. The main run (ids 4..33) must be sized so the week stays ≤ 29.5 h. If it doesn't fit before the 00:00Z reset, run it after the reset. Never let it overlap the dec 055 submit window.

